3. Compute the product modulo 10, ignoring factors of 2 and 5: \[
3 \times 3 \times 1 \times 9 \times 7 \times 3 \equiv 3 \times 3 \times 9 \times 7 \times 3 \equiv 9 \times 9 \times 7 \times 3 \equiv 1 \times 7 \times 3 \equiv 7 \times 3 \equiv 21 \equiv 1 \pmod{10}
\]

Finally, multiply by the remaining factor of 2 from \( 20 \): \[
2 \times 1 \equiv 2 \pmod{10}
\]
